  "goodToKnow": "Das Ungeziefer is vermin or pests, a collective noun for lice, bedbugs, cockroaches and similar creatures. It originally meant an unclean animal unfit for sacrifice. In Kafka's Die Verwandlung (1915), Gregor Samsa wakes up transformed into ein ungeheures Ungeziefer, a monstrous vermin. Nazi propaganda used the word to dehumanise people, so it's avoided for humans. It has no plural."
